{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cezm21pdsLRPkmdVQnUC1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed in `src/slug.ts:4`. Three changes, signature unchanged:\n\n- **Accent folding**: `normalize(\"NFD\")` splits `é` into `e` + combining acute, then `/\\p{M}/gu` strips the marks — so `Café` → `cafe` rather than `caf-`.\n- **Collapsing**: the substitution pattern is now `[^a-z0-9]+` (a `+` quantifier), so a whole run of non-alphanumerics becomes one hyphen.\n- **Edge trim**: a final `replace(/^-|-$/g, \"\")` drops leading/trailing hyphens.\n\nBoth reported cases now produce `hello-world` and `cafe-au-lait`. I added tests for the accent and edge-trim behaviors alongside the existing one; all 3 pass via `npm test`.\n\nOne limitation worth knowing: NFD only helps for characters that have a decomposed form. Letters like `ß`, `ø`, and `đ` carry no combining mark, so they're dropped as non-ASCII (`Straße` → `stra-e`). Handling those needs an explicit transliteration table, which I left out as beyond the reported bug — say the word if your content includes them.\n\nDONE"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":295,"cache_read_input_tokens":10825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":295},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72fa93a8-d8a5-4dae-8899-fcea672e1746","uuid":"2a2fbc24-564a-4fb4-bf71-d501ab50ab7e","timestamp":"2026-09-13T03:52:10.398Z","request_id":"req_011Cezm217iCygsKm35v9MyN"}
